I know exactly why this is happening!
When you click the "Next" page arrow, the detailLoading state becomes true for a split second while the data fetches. Because the Export Excel button currently has disabled={detailLoading}, it temporarily turns itself off. In Material-UI, **disabled buttons turn grey**, which makes it look like it's suddenly flashing a background color!
Since the "Export Excel" API fetches the *entire* batch directly from the backend database regardless of what page you are viewing, it is completely safe to leave the button fully enabled while the table changes pages.
Here is the quick fix to stop the flashing background color. You can apply this to **both** JournalAuthorization.js and JournalPostingStatus.js.
### Fix the Export Excel Button
Find your View Details Modal's <DialogTitle> in both files (around line 520 in Authorization and line 435 in Status).
Look for the Export Excel <Button> and remove detailLoading || from its disabled property.
**Find this:**
```javascript
            <Button 
              variant="outlined" 
              size="small" 
              startIcon={<FileDownloadIcon />} 
              onClick={handleDownloadExcel}
              disabled={detailLoading || !viewingBatchId} // <--- This is causing the grey flash
              sx={{ textTransform: "none", borderRadius: 1.5 }}
            >
              Export Excel
            </Button>

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
            <Button 
              variant="outlined" 
              size="small" 
              startIcon={<FileDownloadIcon />} 
              onClick={handleDownloadExcel}
              disabled={!viewingBatchId} // <--- Removed detailLoading
              sx={{ textTransform: "none", borderRadius: 1.5 }}
            >
              Export Excel
            </Button>

```
Once you remove detailLoading, the button will stay perfectly crisp, outlined, and white even when you click the Next arrow!
